//RS /// Result-arena Option handle (`result_is_ok` / `result_get_i64`), *not* the
//RS /// packed `0 / value + 1` carrier its sibling `jet_jit_list_get_opt` returns.
//RS ///
//RS /// The arena carrier is required, not incidental: a map value is an arbitrary
//RS /// i64, so packing it as `value + 1` would alias a `-1` payload onto `None`.
//RS /// Function values make that concrete — `bind_jit_callable` hands out
//RS /// `-(index + 1)`, so the very first callable stored in a map has the handle
//RS /// `-1`. Keeping presence in a separate `ok` bit is what makes any payload,
//RS /// including `i64::MAX` and every negative handle, representable.
